## jira__sprint_enhanced

    - name: jira__sprint_enhanced
      description: Enhanced sprint metrics aggregated from daily sprint issue history
      grain: One row per sprint_id
      source_models:
      - marts.jira__daily_sprint_issue_history
      business_logic: 'Build sprint-level metrics from marts.jira__daily_sprint_issue_history: - Sprint metadata: Keep distinct combinations of sprint_id, sprint_name, sprint_started_at, sprint_ended_at, sprint_completed_at, board_id, original_estimate_seconds, remaining_estimate_seconds, and time_spent_seconds. - Sprint issue metrics (evaluated across all daily rows for the sprint_id): - sprint_issues: count distinct issue_id across all days. - sprint_assignees: count distinct assignee_user_id across all days (NULL user_ids are not counted). - open_sprint_issues: count distinct issues that are marked as sprint-active and open on any recorded day. - resolved_sprint_issues: count distinct issues whose resolution timestamp is on or before the sprint end and for which there is at least one daily record on or after the resolution date (distinct prevents multi-day double counting). - Commit-at-start metrics (snapshot at sprint start, or today''s snapshot for future-start sprints): - Filter rows where date_day equals the sprint start date, or where date_day equals today and the sprint start date is in the future. - story_points_committed and story_point_estimate_committed: sum values with per-row NULL treated as 0. - issues_committed: count distinct issue_id in the filtered set. - If no rows match this filter for a sprint_id, these fields are NULL after the LEFT JOIN. - End-of-sprint metrics (snapshot on the sprint end date): - Filter rows where date_day equals the sprint end date. - story_points_end and story_point_estimate_end: sum values with per-row NULL treated as 0. - story_points_completed and story_point_estimate_completed: sum values only for rows where the issue is marked resolved-in-sprint; NULL values are ignored by the SUM; if the end snapshot exists but none qualify, the sum is 0; if no end snapshot exists, the value is NULL. - Final assembly: - LEFT JOIN the issue, start, and end metrics to the metadata by sprint_id. - For original_estimate_seconds, remaining_estimate_seconds, and time_spent_seconds, sum across all distinct metadata rows for each sprint_id, treating NULL as 0; other selected fields are carried through to produce one row per sprint_id.'
      columns:
      - name: sprint_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Sprint primary key from daily history; grouping key for all metrics
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: sprint_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Sprint name from daily history
      - name: sprint_started_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Sprint planned start timestamp from daily history
      - name: sprint_ended_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Sprint planned end timestamp from daily history
      - name: sprint_completed_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Timestamp when the sprint was completed (may be NULL if not completed)
      - name: board_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Board identifier associated with the sprint
      - name: story_points_committed
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Sum of story_points at the start snapshot or today's snapshot for future sprints; per-row NULLs treated as 0; NULL if no start snapshot
      - name: story_point_estimate_committed
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Sum of story_point_estimate at the start snapshot or today's snapshot for future sprints; per-row NULLs treated as 0; NULL if no start snapshot
      - name: story_points_end
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Sum of story_points on the sprint end date; per-row NULLs treated as 0; NULL if no end snapshot
      - name: story_point_estimate_end
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Sum of story_point_estimate on the sprint end date; per-row NULLs treated as 0; NULL if no end snapshot
      - name: story_points_completed
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Sum of story_points for issues marked resolved in the sprint on the end snapshot; 0 if snapshot exists but none qualify; NULL if no end snapshot
      - name: story_point_estimate_completed
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Sum of story_point_estimate for issues marked resolved in the sprint on the end snapshot; 0 if snapshot exists but none qualify; NULL if no end snapshot
      - name: sprint_assignees
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Distinct assignee_user_id count across all daily rows (NULLs not counted)
      - name: sprint_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Distinct issue_id count across all daily rows for the sprint_id
      - name: issues_committed
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Distinct issue count at the start snapshot; NULL if no start snapshot
      - name: open_sprint_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Distinct issues active in the sprint and open on any recorded day
      - name: resolved_sprint_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Distinct issues resolved on or before sprint end and with a daily record on or after their resolution date
      - name: original_estimate_seconds
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Sum of original_estimate_seconds across distinct metadata rows; NULLs treated as 0; unit seconds
      - name: remaining_estimate_seconds
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Sum of remaining_estimate_seconds across distinct metadata rows; NULLs treated as 0; unit seconds
      - name: time_spent_seconds
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Sum of time_spent_seconds across distinct metadata rows; NULLs treated as 0; unit seconds


## jira__daily_sprint_issue_history

    - name: jira__daily_sprint_issue_history
      description: Daily issue-level sprint history built from a global date spine, enriched with current issue fields and deterministic sprint/issue status flags for burndown
      grain: One row per sprint_id + issue_id + date_day
      source_models:
      - intermediate.int_jira__issue_sprint
      - marts.jira__issue_enhanced
      - staging.stg_jira__issue
      business_logic: '- Build sprint_issue_mapping from intermediate.int_jira__issue_sprint by keeping rows with a non-null current_sprint_id and selecting sprint_id, issue_id, issue_key, sprint_name, sprint_started_at, sprint_ended_at, sprint_completed_at, and board_id. - Create a global date spine: - start_date is the earliest issue creation date across staging.stg_jira__issue. - end_date is the latest of the issue resolution date, or today for unresolved issues. - Generate one date_day for each calendar day from start_date through end_date inclusive. - For each date_day, set date_week to (year of date_day) * 100 + (week-of-year of date_day). - Cross join the mapping with the date spine and retain only days on or after the sprint start date; include days up to seven days after the sprint end when an end date exists; if the end date is missing, keep all days on or after the start date. - Enrich each row by joining marts.jira__issue_enhanced on issue_id to bring the current, non-historical fields: issue_created_at, issue_resolved_at, assignee_user_id, assignee_name, original_estimate_seconds, remaining_estimate_seconds, time_spent_seconds, and status. - Derive story_points deterministically from a hash of issue_id: compute r = abs(hash(issue_id) mod 10); map r=0→8, r=1→5, r=2→3, r=3→2, r=4→1; all other r values yield NULL; copy story_points into story_point_estimate. - Per-day flags: - is_sprint_active is true on and after the sprint start date and, when present, through the sprint end date; otherwise false. - is_sprint_completed is true on and after the sprint completion date when present; otherwise false. - is_issue_open is true on and after the issue creation date only while the issue has no resolution timestamp; otherwise false. - is_issue_resolved_in_sprint is true on and after the resolution date when the resolution occurred on or before the sprint end; otherwise false. - days_left_in_sprint is the whole-day difference between the sprint end date and date_day when date_day is within the sprint start–end window (inclusive); otherwise NULL; zero on the end date. - Generate sprint_issue_day_id as a stable 64-bit hash of the string "date_day|sprint_id|issue_id", with date_day formatted as YYYY-MM-DD and "|" as the delimiter. - Return all columns and order rows by sprint_id, issue_id, and date_day.'
      columns:
      - name: sprint_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Sprint identifier from int_jira__issue_sprint.current_sprint_id; not null due to filter
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: issue_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Issue identifier; join key to jira__issue_enhanced; not null
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: issue_key
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Human-readable issue key from int_jira__issue_sprint; not null
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: date_day
        data_type: DATE
        description: Calendar day from the global date spine; one row per sprint_id+issue_id+date_day; not null
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: date_week
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Week index computed as (year of date_day)*100 + (week-of-year of date_day); deterministic
      - name: sprint_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Sprint name from int_jira__issue_sprint.current_sprint_name; not null
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: sprint_started_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Sprint start timestamp; bounds rows where date_day is on or after the start date
      - name: sprint_ended_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Sprint end timestamp; daily rows extend through seven days after the end date; may be null
      - name: sprint_completed_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Sprint completion timestamp; used for is_sprint_completed; may be null
      - name: board_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Jira board identifier associated with the sprint; may be null
      - name: issue_created_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Issue creation timestamp from jira__issue_enhanced.created_at; not null
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: issue_resolved_at
        data_type: TIMESTAMP
        description: Issue resolution timestamp from jira__issue_enhanced; null if unresolved; used in flags
      - name: assignee_user_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Assignee user identifier from jira__issue_enhanced; may be null
      - name: assignee_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Assignee display name from jira__issue_enhanced; may be null
      - name: original_estimate_seconds
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Original time estimate in seconds from jira__issue_enhanced; non-negative when present; null allowed
        tests:
        - original_estimate_seconds IS NULL OR original_estimate_seconds >= 0
      - name: remaining_estimate_seconds
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Remaining time estimate in seconds from jira__issue_enhanced; non-negative when present; null allowed
        tests:
        - remaining_estimate_seconds IS NULL OR remaining_estimate_seconds >= 0
      - name: time_spent_seconds
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Time spent in seconds from jira__issue_enhanced; non-negative when present; null allowed
        tests:
        - time_spent_seconds IS NULL OR time_spent_seconds >= 0
      - name: status
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Current issue status from jira__issue_enhanced.current_status; static across dates (no historical tracking)
      - name: story_points
        data_type: INTEGER
        description: 'Deterministic pseudo-story points based on issue_id hash: r=0→8, r=1→5, r=2→3, r=3→2, r=4→1; other r values yield null'
        tests:
        - story_points IS NULL OR story_points >= 0
      - name: story_point_estimate
        data_type: INTEGER
        description: Exact copy of story_points for convenience; same null and value semantics
        tests:
        - story_point_estimate IS NULL OR story_point_estimate >= 0
      - name: is_sprint_active
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: True when date_day is on or after the sprint start date and, when present, on or before the sprint end date; else false
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: is_sprint_completed
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: True when a sprint completion timestamp exists and date_day is on or after that date; else false
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: is_issue_open
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: True when date_day is on or after issue_created_at and there is no resolution timestamp; else false
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: is_issue_resolved_in_sprint
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: True on and after the resolution date when a resolution exists and it occurred on or before the sprint end; else false
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: days_left_in_sprint
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Whole days remaining until the sprint end when date_day is within the sprint start–end window (inclusive); else null; zero on the end date; non-negative
        tests:
        - days_left_in_sprint IS NULL OR days_left_in_sprint >= 0
      - name: sprint_issue_day_id
        data_type: UBIGINT
        description: Unsigned 64-bit hash of the string 'date_day|sprint_id|issue_id' using '|' as the delimiter and date_day formatted as YYYY-MM-DD; stable; not null
        tests:
        - not_null


## jira__team_performance_dashboard_simple

    - name: jira__team_performance_dashboard_simple
      description: Simplified team performance view joining user metrics to user profile; includes users with >0 closed issues and a constant performance_tier
      grain: One row per matching user_id across metrics and user profile where count_closed_issues > 0; duplicates from either source produce multiple rows
      source_models:
      - intermediate.int_jira__user_metrics
      - staging.stg_jira__user
      business_logic: '- Start from intermediate.int_jira__user_metrics as um. - Inner join staging.stg_jira__user as u on um.user_id equals u.user_id (rows with NULL user_id on either side do not match). - Keep rows where um.count_closed_issues is greater than 0 (NULLs are excluded by the filter). - Select: um.user_id, u.user_display_name, u.email, um.count_closed_issues, um.count_open_issues, um.avg_close_time_days, and the constant ''Standard User'' as performance_tier. - Order the result by um.count_closed_issues descending; ties have no defined secondary ordering. Persisted outputs may not retain order; apply ORDER BY at query time to reproduce.'
      columns:
      - name: user_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: User identifier from int_jira__user_metrics; non-NULL due to inner join equality
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: user_display_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Display name from stg_jira__user; passed through as stored; may be NULL
      - name: email
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Email from stg_jira__user; passed through as stored; may be NULL
      - name: count_closed_issues
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Closed issues count from int_jira__user_metrics; strictly greater than 0 due to the filter
      - name: count_open_issues
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Open issues count from int_jira__user_metrics; passed through as stored; may be NULL or zero
      - name: avg_close_time_days
        data_type: DECIMAL(18,0)
        description: Average issue close time in days from int_jira__user_metrics; scale 0; may be NULL
      - name: performance_tier
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Constant value 'Standard User' for every row; non-NULL; exact casing preserved


## jira__issue_intelligence_simple

    - name: jira__issue_intelligence_simple
      description: Simplified issue intelligence with risk and completion probability derived from issue age and resolution
      grain: One row per issue_id
      source_models:
      - marts.jira__issue_enhanced (issue_id, issue_key, issue_name, project_name, assignee_name, current_status, open_duration_seconds, resolved_at)
      business_logic: '- Source rows from marts.jira__issue_enhanced; no filtering or deduplication. - Pass through identifiers and context: issue_id, issue_key, issue_name, project_name, assignee_name, current_status. - Compute lifecycle_days by converting open_duration_seconds to days (divide by 86,400); fractional value; NULL propagates; no rounding. - Assign risk_level using strict thresholds for unresolved issues: - If resolved_at is NULL and open duration is more than 90 days → High Risk. - Else if resolved_at is NULL and open duration is more than 30 days → Medium Risk. - Else → Low Risk. Resolved issues are always Low Risk; unresolved with NULL duration is Low Risk. - Compute completion_probability: - If resolved_at is NOT NULL → 1.0. - Else if open duration is 7 days or less → 0.9. - Else if open duration is 30 days or less → 0.7. - Else → 0.3. Unresolved with NULL duration yields 0.3; values emitted with one decimal place. - Order rows by open_duration_seconds descending; no secondary sort; NULL positioning follows database default.'
      columns:
      - name: issue_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Unique issue identifier; one output row per issue_id
        tests:
        - not_null
        - unique
      - name: issue_key
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Readable issue key (e.g., PROJ-123)
      - name: issue_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Issue summary/title
      - name: project_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Project name
      - name: assignee_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Assignee name; NULL if unassigned
      - name: current_status
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Current workflow status
      - name: lifecycle_days
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Open duration in days; seconds divided by 86,400; fractional; NULL if source is NULL; no rounding
      - name: risk_level
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: 'Risk bucket: unresolved and >90 days → High Risk; unresolved and >30 days → Medium Risk; otherwise Low Risk; resolved always Low Risk'
      - name: completion_probability
        data_type: DECIMAL(2,1)
        description: Completion probability mapped to 1.0, 0.9, 0.7, or 0.3 based on resolution and age; unresolved with NULL duration → 0.3


## jira__project_risk_simple

    - name: jira__project_risk_simple
      description: Executive-friendly project risk and value labels derived from Jira metrics joined to project names via inner join; rows are ordered by open issues descending.
      grain: One row per project_id present in both source tables (inner join)
      source_models:
      - intermediate.int_jira__project_metrics
      - staging.stg_jira__project
      business_logic: '- Inner join intermediate.int_jira__project_metrics (pm) with staging.stg_jira__project (p) on project_id; only projects present in both sources are included. - Selected fields: pm.project_id, p.project_name, pm.count_closed_issues, pm.count_open_issues, pm.avg_close_time_days (integral day count as provided). - Risk category precedence: 1) High Risk if open issues are more than twice the closed issues. 2) Otherwise, Medium Risk if the average close time in days is greater than 30. 3) Otherwise, Low Risk. Null handling: any null in the compared fields makes the check fail; if both checks fail, the result is Low Risk. - Project value: 1) High Value if closed issues are greater than 50. 2) Otherwise, Medium Value if closed issues are greater than 20. 3) Otherwise, Standard Value. Null handling: a null closed-issue count results in Standard Value. - Final ordering: sort by count_open_issues in descending order; no secondary sort, filtering, rounding, or de-duplication beyond the inner join.'
      columns:
      - name: project_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Project identifier from metrics used as the inner-join key.
        tests:
        - not_null
        - unique
      - name: project_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Project name from the project staging table, carried through unchanged.
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: count_closed_issues
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Total closed issues from metrics; used to determine risk (twice-open check) and value tiers; nulls are allowed and not transformed.
      - name: count_open_issues
        data_type: HUGEINT
        description: Total open issues from metrics; used for the high-risk check; nulls are allowed and not transformed.
      - name: avg_close_time_days
        data_type: DECIMAL(18,0)
        description: Average issue resolution time in whole days from metrics; nulls allowed; no rounding performed here.
      - name: risk_category
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: High Risk if open issues exceed twice closed; else Medium Risk if average close time is over 30 days; otherwise Low Risk; null comparisons default to Low Risk.
        tests:
        - not_null
        - risk_category IN ('High Risk', 'Medium Risk', 'Low Risk')
      - name: project_value
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: High Value if closed issues exceed 50; else Medium Value if over 20; otherwise Standard Value; null closed-issue counts default to Standard Value.
        tests:
        - not_null
        - project_value IN ('High Value', 'Medium Value', 'Standard Value')


## jira__team_performance_dashboard

    - name: jira__team_performance_dashboard
      description: Team performance dashboard per user aggregated across all projects with activity, delivery, collaboration, growth, risk, and scoring metrics
      grain: One row per user_id (project_id='all_projects')
      source_models:
      - intermediate.int_jira__user_metrics
      - staging.stg_jira__user
      - staging.stg_jira__issue
      - staging.stg_jira__issue_link
      - staging.stg_jira__comment
      - staging.stg_jira__sprint
      - staging.stg_jira__issue_field_history
      - staging.stg_jira__field
      - raw.issue_sprint_history
      business_logic: '- Build user_activity_summary: - Join user metrics to users on user_id; emit one row per user with project_id=''all_projects'' and project_name=''All Projects''. - Set current_engagement_tier=''Standard User'', current_pattern_type=''Regular User'', current_lifecycle_stage=''Stable''. - Set avg_daily_activity_score and avg_weekly_activity_score from average close time days; avg_consistency_score=0.7; last_active_date=current_date; active_days_count=30; churn_risk_days=0; productive_days=count_closed_issues; highly_active_days=count_closed_issues if >10 else 0. - Build team_collaboration_metrics from issues created in the last 90 days and with a non-null assignee: - Group by project_id and assignee_user_id. - total_assigned_issues counts assigned issues. - resolved_issues counts assigned issues with a resolution date. - avg_resolution_days averages the days between creation and resolution over resolved issues. - high_priority_issues counts assigned issues with a non-null priority. - bug_issues counts assigned issues with a non-null issue type (label is generic, not limited to “Bug”). - epic_issues counts assigned issues with a non-null parent issue. - Join issue links and count distinct linked issue references on both sides; join comments and count distinct non-assignee comment authors. - estimate_accuracy_ratio averages the absolute relative difference between time spent and original estimate over issues where both values are present and >0. - Build sprint_participation_analysis from recent sprints (started within 180 days), issues, and derived story points: - Parse numeric story points from active field history where the field name contains “story” and “point”; default to 1 when no number is found. - Group by sprint_id, sprint_name, assignee user_id, and project_id. - Measure issues_in_sprint, issues_completed_in_sprint (resolved within sprint window), total_story_points, story_points_completed_in_sprint, and avg_completion_day_in_sprint (days from sprint start to resolution when resolved on/before sprint end). - Build user_growth_metrics by left joining user_activity_summary to issues and comments: - Consider issues where the user is assignee, reporter, or creator; and comments authored by the user. - first_issue_date is the earliest issue creation date; last_resolved_date is the latest resolution date. - days_since_first_issue is the days from current_date to first_issue_date. - issue_types_worked_on counts distinct issue types; priority_levels_handled counts distinct priorities; projects_contributed_to counts distinct projects. - issues_reported counts issues reported by the user; issues_commented_on counts distinct issues the user commented on. - Build team_performance_scoring by left joining user_activity_summary to team_collaboration_metrics, user_growth_metrics, and aggregated sprint metrics: - Aggregate sprint metrics per user and project: sprint_count (distinct sprints), avg_sprint_completion_rate (average of per-sprint completed/issues; sprints with zero issues are excluded), total_story_points_delivered (sum of completed story points). - Rounding and units: - avg_daily_activity_score and avg_weekly_activity_score are computed to two decimals but stored without fractional part due to column type. - consistency_percentage = avg_consistency_score × 100 rounded to one decimal. - resolution_rate_percentage = percentage of assigned issues resolved, rounded to one decimal; NULL if no assigned issues. - avg_resolution_days rounded to one decimal; NULL if no resolved issues. - estimate_accuracy_percentage = estimate_accuracy_ratio × 100 rounded to one decimal; NULL if no eligible issues. - Risk flags: at_churn_risk is true when churn_risk_days > 7; inactive_recently is true when current_date − last_active_date > 7 days; poor_estimation is true when estimate accuracy ratio > 2; all flags are always populated (no NULLs). - Note: Joins to collaboration and sprint metrics use (user_id, project_id); because project_id=''all_projects'', these often remain NULL. - Final scoring and tiering: - overall_performance_score clamps to 0–100 and sums components: - Delivery (40%): 40/30/20/10/0 points at resolution rate ≥90/≥75/≥60/≥40/else. - Activity (30%): 30/20/10/0 points for engagement tier Highly/Moderately/Lightly Active/else. - Quality (20%): 20/15/10/5 points for estimate accuracy in [80,120]/[70,130]/[60,140]/else. - Collaboration (10%): 10/7/5/0 points at unique collaborators ≥5/≥3/≥1/else. - performance_tier: Top Performer (score ≥85), Strong Performer (≥70), Average Performer (≥50), else Needs Improvement. - Final output is ordered by overall_performance_score descending, then project_name, then user_display_name.'
      columns:
      - name: user_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: User identifier; grouping key; exactly one output row per user_id
        tests:
        - not_null
        - unique
      - name: user_display_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Display name from staging.stg_jira__user for the user_id
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: email
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Email from staging.stg_jira__user; may be NULL if not present
      - name: project_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Constant 'all_projects' emitted for every user row
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: project_name
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Constant 'All Projects' emitted for every user row
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: current_engagement_tier
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Engagement tier label set to 'Standard User'; used in scoring only when equal to 'Highly Active', 'Moderately Active', or 'Lightly Active'
      - name: current_pattern_type
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Activity pattern label; constant 'Regular User'
      - name: current_lifecycle_stage
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Lifecycle stage label; constant 'Stable'
      - name: avg_daily_activity_score
        data_type: DECIMAL(18,0)
        description: Derived from average close time days; computed to two decimals then stored without fractional part
      - name: avg_weekly_activity_score
        data_type: DECIMAL(18,0)
        description: Derived from average close time days; computed to two decimals then stored without fractional part
      - name: consistency_percentage
        data_type: DECIMAL(12,1)
        description: Activity consistency expressed as a percentage rounded to one decimal; constant 70.0 in current logic
      - name: total_assigned_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Count of issues assigned to the user in the last 90 days; NULL when no (user_id, project_id) match to collaboration metrics due to project_id='all_projects'
      - name: resolved_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Count of assigned issues with a resolution date in the last 90 days; NULL when no (user_id, project_id) match to collaboration metrics
      - name: resolution_rate_percentage
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Percentage of assigned issues resolved in the last 90 days, rounded to one decimal; NULL if no assigned issues
      - name: avg_resolution_days
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Average days from issue creation to resolution for resolved issues in the last 90 days, rounded to one decimal; NULL if none
      - name: high_priority_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Count of assigned issues with a non-null priority in the last 90 days; NULL when no (user_id, project_id) match to collaboration metrics
      - name: performance_tier
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: 'Tier based on overall_performance_score: Top Performer (≥85), Strong Performer (≥70), Average Performer (≥50), else Needs Improvement'
      - name: bug_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Count of assigned issues with a non-null issue type in the last 90 days (generic, not limited to 'Bug'); NULL when no match
      - name: epic_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Count of assigned issues with a non-null parent issue in the last 90 days; NULL when no match
      - name: estimate_accuracy_percentage
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Average relative deviation between time spent and original estimate over issues with both values >0, expressed as a percentage and rounded to one decimal; higher is worse; NULL if no eligible issues
      - name: linked_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Total distinct linked issue references (issue_id plus related_issue_id) for the user's assigned issues in the last 90 days; NULL when no match
      - name: unique_collaborators_on_issues
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Distinct non-assignee comment authors on the user's assigned issues in the last 90 days; NULL when no match
      - name: projects_contributed_to
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Distinct projects across issues where the user is assignee, reporter, or creator; 0 if none
      - name: issue_types_worked_on
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Distinct issue types across issues where the user is assignee, reporter, or creator; 0 if none
      - name: sprint_count
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Distinct sprint count aggregated per (user_id, project_id); NULL when no match because project_id='all_projects'
      - name: avg_sprint_completion_rate
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Average per-sprint completion ratio (completed issues divided by issues in sprint), excluding sprints with zero issues; NULL when no matching sprint data for the user and project
      - name: total_story_points_delivered
        data_type: DECIMAL(38,3)
        description: Sum of story points completed within sprints per (user_id, project_id); NULL when no match because project_id='all_projects'
      - name: days_since_first_issue
        data_type: DOUBLE
        description: Days between current_date and the user's first observed issue creation date; NULL if the user has no issues
      - name: leadership_indicator
        data_type: BIGINT
        description: Count of issues reported by the user; 0 if none
      - name: at_churn_risk
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: True when churn_risk_days > 7; False otherwise; always populated
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: inactive_recently
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: True when current_date minus last_active_date exceeds 7 days; False otherwise; always populated
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: poor_estimation
        data_type: BOOLEAN
        description: True when the estimate accuracy ratio exceeds 2; False otherwise or when unavailable; always populated
        tests:
        - not_null
      - name: overall_performance_score
        data_type: INTEGER
        description: Composite score (0–100) from delivery, activity, quality, and collaboration components; clamped to 0–100 using defined thresholds
        tests:
        - not_null


## jira__daily_issue_field_history

    - name: jira__daily_issue_field_history
      description: Simplified per-row snapshot using the created_at date; fields copied from int_jira__issue_join with status name joined from staging via left join.
      grain: One row per source row in intermediate.int_jira__issue_join (issue_id may repeat)
      source_models:
      - intermediate.int_jira__issue_join
      - staging.stg_jira__status
      business_logic: '- Create a base set from intermediate.int_jira__issue_join: issue_id; date_day = the date part of created_at; date_week = same as date_day; assignee = assignee_user_id; reporter = reporter_user_id; priority = priority_id; issue_type = issue_type_id; components, story_points, and story_point_estimate are set to NULL; carry status_id for joining. - Left join to staging.stg_jira__status to add status name by matching status_id as text on both sides; if no match, status is NULL. - Compute issue_day_id by hashing the string formed as date_day + "|" + issue_id (in that order); if date_day or issue_id is NULL, issue_day_id is NULL. - No aggregation, filtering, or sorting; output preserves one row per input row; string values keep original casing and spacing unless set to NULL above.'
      columns:
      - name: date_day
        data_type: DATE
        description: Date part of created_at; NULL if created_at is NULL.
      - name: date_week
        data_type: DATE
        description: Equal to date_day; no weekly rollup.
      - name: issue_id
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Issue identifier from intermediate.int_jira__issue_join; may be NULL.
      - name: status
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Status name joined from staging.stg_jira__status by status_id; NULL if no match.
      - name: components
        data_type: INTEGER
        description: Always NULL in this model.
      - name: issue_type
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Issue type identifier copied from issue_type_id; may be NULL.
      - name: assignee
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Assignee user identifier from assignee_user_id; may be NULL.
      - name: reporter
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Reporter user identifier from reporter_user_id; may be NULL.
      - name: priority
        data_type: VARCHAR
        description: Priority identifier from priority_id; may be NULL.
      - name: story_points
        data_type: INTEGER
        description: Always NULL in this model.
      - name: story_point_estimate
        data_type: INTEGER
        description: Always NULL in this model.
      - name: issue_day_id
        data_type: UBIGINT
        description: Deterministic hash of date_day and issue_id joined by '|' in that order; NULL if either input is NULL.




